WEBVTT

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.600
Hey, Tsutomu! Tell me what one plus one is.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.430
Duh... Two.

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:26.430
What's this about?

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:30.840
My club. I joined the cinematography club.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.120
Why don't you join too?

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:35.680
Well...

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.120
Hey, Senkawa!

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:42.350
Cinematography Club, huh? I think you'll like this better.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.100
<i>Teacher After School</i>
<i>"I'll give you a personal lesson"</i>
<i>She'll turn you on!</i>

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.370
We're going over to my place to look at these.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:51.600
Maybe it's too much for him to handle.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:52.520
Perhaps.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:54.000
Hey! You guys!

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:58.030
Don't push that smut onto Tsutomu, all right?

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.060
But these are the important things he needs to learn.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:04.480
It's so true.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.200
Are these the things you want to learn, Tsutomu Senkawa?!

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.570
Why, of course! Right?!

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:15.050
You wanted to look at those pictures, didn't you?

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:16.850
Don't be ridiculous.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.030
How can I with you around?

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.550
Why is that? Think you're going to feel funny?

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:25.340
Enough already. Besides, we have more important things to deal with.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:29.340
That's right. Hustle, boy, hustle!

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:47.130
The results couldn't be worse, just as you predicted.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:50.110
After comparing your sample with that of the Fonted incident...

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:53.150
It seems that Revi has developed a more potent drug than was used before.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:56.530
The Fonted incident... You means it's that serum?

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.040
That's right.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:03.920
As you know, Altirrans are somewhat immune to the serum.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:07.560
But for humans, the consequences are catastrophic.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:10.150
If it enters the cellular structure of humans...

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:16.100
it affects the genes, regenerating the nervous system, and causing mutation.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.330
Mutation... You mean genetic mutation?

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:19.840
That's right.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:24.340
Then comes the possibility of a superhuman psy power.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:29.330
I think Revi has already developed this serum.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.190
Is there some type of antidote for it?

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:45.900
The only thing you can do is perhaps use the hyper-resolve.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.200
But it doesn't exist here.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:54.550
Then we'll just have to thwart their plans first. That's perhaps all we can do.

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:05.490
What's this?

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:10.280
Just a little gadget.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:30.450
This is all that we were able to recover.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.990
Send Revi this message...

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.630
The android was of no use to us.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.370
Instead of Ms. Revi's "elite androids,"

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:45.580
the use of one of my retro- soldiers is indeed required.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.900
You just don't understand, do you?

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:58.930
You are quite insensitive to Ms. Revi's affection for these androids.

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:02.940
She'll come around, don't worry about it.

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.310
I guess I'll be going now.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:12.050
I'm sorry about your sister.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.830
Thank you for your condolences.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.410
Well, shall we begin?

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:36.620
Yes, I know him.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:40.580
He was with my father when my father was medical chief.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:44.580
They say he was the best in nuclear medicine.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.640
Has something happened?

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:50.290
Of course we could be completely off-track.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.570
But we thought we'd look into any leads, promising or not.

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:55.320
Is that right?

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:58.300
Is there anything you can tell us about Hikawa's past?

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:03.590
My father said that he went to the States right after the war ended.

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:08.100
Something about doing research at a military laboratory.

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:13.780
He returned to us after working on some treatments.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.610
Can you tell us anything at all about after he retired?

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:21.860
I think I have his address of about three years ago.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:25.700
After all, he did have some surgery done here.

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:29.630
Thanks for your help. I'm very sorry for putting you through all this trouble.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:37.930
That's it over there.

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:05.020
This is recent.

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:28.970
You know what this is?

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:33.990
I think I've seen this before...

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:39.260
Um, I think it's a...

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:02.730
Damn it!

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:04.750
That really makes me mad!

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:09.060
I figured it out. I know what it is!

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:11.630
It's a map of the water system!

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:15.300
It shows all the pipes and aqueducts for the water supply!

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:19.730
Oh no. They're going to put that serum in the water supply.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:24.140
If that happens, thousands, no, millions will be affected!

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:30.890
Yes. I understand.

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:34.780
It's confirmed. We now have control of all facilities, Ms. Revi.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:59.500
Hey, you there!

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:02.660
Tsutomu Senkawa?

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:06.350
What's with you?

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:09.380
Well, uh, nothing really.

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:13.380
What's the matter, Tsutomu?

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:15.780
I'm scared.

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:18.410
What's the matter with you!? Get yourself together!

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:22.900
But aren't there a whole bunch of them taking over?

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:25.730
Like those Arkazoid guys or something?

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:26.760
Yeah, probably.

00:09:27.070 --> 00:09:31.620
But it's just you to fight them. There's got to be some other way.

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:32.700
None!

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:34.430
Oh, MAN!

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:42.940
Sure we have enough serum?

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:47.500
There's no point in explaining it to you. Just shut up and watch.

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:59.370
So that's where Seichiro Hikawa lives?

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:03.440
That's my understanding.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:25.620
That's an Arkazoid.

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:27.540
I thought so.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:32.520
<i>Solar-powered "Clean Energy"</i>
<i>purifies your water!</i>

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:30.730
What are you doing? Trying to run away?!

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:32.520
Just hold on a second. Let's think about this some more.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:35.330
Just hold on a second. Let's think about this some more.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.390
We'll miss our chance if we play games like this.

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:41.370
If we don't act now, even Natsumi's going to turn into a monster.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:44.420
Don't you at least want to protect her?!

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:07.600
Hey, you!

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:14.340
I said, this is restricted to authorized personnel only. Leave now.

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:19.230
What about you, mister? I know what you're doing here.

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:24.100
This is... very unfortunate.

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:39.660
Well, well. So this is that dog from the Federation.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.180
That's me!

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:54.140
Let's go!

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:27.420
All the neighbors say that they haven't seen him in about three years.

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:33.630
Apparently, Seichiro Hikawa lived here all by himself until then.

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:40.680
This sure is a creepy room though.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.750
It doesn't seem like anyone lives here now.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:04.150
What is it?

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:09.140
<i>July 3rd. Those people who</i> <i>recently visited have returned.</i>

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:13.670
<i>They seem particularly</i> <i>interested in my past research.</i>

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:16.930
<i>July 16th. This is incredible.</i>

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:20.240
<i>It seems the molt that the</i> <i>visitors brought may be able to...</i>

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:24.530
<i>... enable the realization</i> <i>of all of my research.</i>

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:27.690
<i>July 17th. I have decided.</i>

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:30.930
<i>I will use my own body</i> <i>for this experiment...</i>

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:33.190
<i>... and carry out my dreams</i> <i>of half a century ago.</i>

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:35.850
<i>My new research...</i>

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:41.650
<i>... to create a superior soldier,</i> <i>invincible to all.</i>

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:11.360
<i>Ms. Revi made it all possible.</i>

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:26.890
Big side effect.

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:29.840
You plan on continuing with something that's not ready?

00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:37.510
We're stopping this now. We're pulling you from this project.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:41.520
Who else are you going to find to finish this now?

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:46.840
Don't worry. As long as we have the data, we can get anyone to...

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.660
You can just lie there quietly.

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.980
All right! Release the serum, now!

00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:20.600
Wait a minute!

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:41.960
You think you can stop me!

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:54.960
You really are a nuisance.

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:00.140
So we finally meet.

00:16:00.970 --> 00:16:02.920
That reservoir below you is...

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:05.410
...connected to many millions of water pipes.

00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:11.690
When I open the reservoir valves, the water will flow to all of Tokyo.

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:14.740
Interesting, isn't it?

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:19.410
I will never let it happen.

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:23.420
So, you actually think you can stop me?

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:28.430
And you actually think you can stop me with that thing?

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:52.990
There is no one who can stop me now.

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:56.150
Behold!

00:17:57.030 --> 00:18:01.880
All of the people of Tokyo shall be reborn as retro-soldiers.

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:27.540
Damn!

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:39.150
Stop it!

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:16.190
Birdy, we've got to do something fast.

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:20.380
It's too late now. There's nothing we can do.

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:24.320
What are you saying?! It's no joke! We have to do something!

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:27.510
It's impossible. We can't even do a hyper-resolve.

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:29.660
What's that?

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:34.300
You remember the big flash when we first met?

00:19:37.180 --> 00:19:41.180
It's a device thousands of times more powerful than that.

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:43.230
But such a thing doesn't exist here.

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:52.670
Enough of this playing around.

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:54.850
Die!

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.980
Birdy? Are you all right?

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:34.830
Birdy?

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:39.010
Damn! What am I supposed to do now?

00:20:43.030 --> 00:20:45.010
<i>Clean Energy - High Voltage (60 m)</i>

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:05.160
Birdy!

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:12.340
What is it you're thinking of doing now?

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:14.800
We just need electricity, right?

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:19.070
Let's do it, Birdy. There's nothing else we can do.

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:22.030
But... Are you sure?

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:25.210
I don't know if my body can withstand the power from all that voltage.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.930
If I fail, I know that you cannot be saved this time.

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:32.630
At this rate, Natsumi, my family and my friends...

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:35.390
All the people of Tokyo will turn into monsters!

00:21:35.920 --> 00:21:37.340
I have no choice.

00:21:37.670 --> 00:21:38.390
Tsutomu.

00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:48.680
Let's do it now, Birdy! Hurry!

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:51.190
I believe in you.

00:21:51.530 --> 00:21:53.100
It will all work out.

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:57.540
Really? Do you really think so?

00:21:58.030 --> 00:21:59.670
I have faith.

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:13.700
Ms. Revi, it seems that the plan has failed.

00:23:18.210 --> 00:23:21.620
Salamander, please make the arrangements for tomorrow's flight.

00:23:22.440 --> 00:23:22.920
Yes.

00:23:23.310 --> 00:23:24.290
<i>Investigations</i>

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:26.720
Where's the lieutenant?

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:28.480
He's watching a video over there.

00:23:30.290 --> 00:23:33.200
According to the results of the DNA test on that body...

00:23:33.350 --> 00:23:35.730
There's no mistaking it was Seichiro Hikawa.

00:23:36.250 --> 00:23:37.280
Really.

00:23:38.980 --> 00:23:40.710
What's that? Surveillance?

00:23:41.340 --> 00:23:44.700
It's from the sewer system at the waterworks.

00:23:44.730 --> 00:23:48.110
Everything was erased except for this.

00:23:49.340 --> 00:23:50.930
Wait, that girl!

00:23:51.290 --> 00:23:56.160
This whole thing is just getting more and more confusing.

00:23:57.370 --> 00:23:59.340
Hey, we're out of toilet paper.

00:23:59.400 --> 00:24:03.330
There should be another one there. Just use your eyes.

00:24:04.390 --> 00:24:06.550
Oh, here it is.

00:24:06.990 --> 00:24:11.610
Mother, this isn't the right margarine. I asked for low-fat.

00:24:11.730 --> 00:24:14.050
They didn't have any at the corner store.

00:24:14.300 --> 00:24:16.500
I'll go to the store by the station next time and get some.

00:24:17.850 --> 00:24:21.110
That felt good. Good way to start off the day.

00:24:25.560 --> 00:24:28.360
What? You been doing that all week.

00:24:28.700 --> 00:24:31.830
Can't you do something about that hair?

00:24:32.900 --> 00:24:37.010
Huh? Is this what's popular these days, Hazumi?

00:24:37.140 --> 00:24:38.340
Thanks for the food.

00:24:40.480 --> 00:24:42.140
I'm off.

00:24:43.770 --> 00:24:45.110
Have a good day, dear!

00:24:47.510 --> 00:24:51.750
He's such a kid. Normally guys try to look sexy or something.

00:24:51.770 --> 00:24:54.450
He leaves it as such a mess. Unbelievable.

00:24:54.820 --> 00:24:56.730
I guess the girls will stay clear of him.

00:25:00.940 --> 00:25:05.050
I wonder what they think happened to me?

00:25:05.330 --> 00:25:08.280
Come on. At least it's only the hair.

00:25:08.450 --> 00:25:10.500
Well, I guess...

00:25:16.270 --> 00:25:19.070
Take it easy. I'm not going to do anything.

00:25:19.940 --> 00:25:22.410
Thought I'd come by and say good-bye.

00:25:24.010 --> 00:25:25.000
You won't get away.

00:25:25.430 --> 00:25:28.330
I'm not running away. I will see you again some day.

00:25:29.140 --> 00:25:31.140
Until then, you better improve your skills.

00:25:32.030 --> 00:25:35.030
At your level, you're no match for me right now.

00:25:36.330 --> 00:25:39.450
And that means you'll never get close to Christella Revi.

00:25:41.530 --> 00:25:44.730
We will be leaving this country for some time...

00:25:44.800 --> 00:25:46.240
...and devise our new plans.

00:25:46.850 --> 00:25:49.780
There were a few loose ends on this most recent project.

00:25:50.590 --> 00:25:53.560
What is Christella Revi trying to do here on earth, anyway?

00:25:54.020 --> 00:25:56.760
It is my job to determine what it is that we must do.

00:25:57.520 --> 00:26:01.970
And to determine whether Christella Revi is a Goddess, a devil, or just a criminal.

00:26:02.860 --> 00:26:05.910
I will determine that and take action.

00:26:17.310 --> 00:26:18.920
You're too much of a hothead.

00:26:17.310 --> 00:26:18.920
That is what takes away from your skill.

00:26:19.960 --> 00:26:23.070
Let's hope you'll improve by the time we next meet.

00:26:27.800 --> 00:26:28.670
That man...

00:26:30.430 --> 00:26:33.020
What a strange man he is.

00:26:33.610 --> 00:26:36.740
He has a point about you being a hothead though.

00:26:36.790 --> 00:26:39.040
What?! You going to take his side now?!

00:26:39.140 --> 00:26:40.860
That's not what I meant.

00:26:41.200 --> 00:26:44.930
I might get a little heated at times...

00:26:45.580 --> 00:26:49.860
But anyway, it seems like I'll have to stick around this planet a little longer.

00:26:50.170 --> 00:26:53.500
I guess we'll just have to make the best of it while I'm here.

00:26:53.590 --> 00:26:54.800
Right, Tsutomu?

00:26:56.590 --> 00:26:58.930
You have a problem with that?

00:26:59.150 --> 00:27:00.260
Tsutomu!

00:27:02.910 --> 00:27:05.860
Better hurry, or you're going to be late!

00:27:06.210 --> 00:27:08.710
Oh, no!

00:27:13.990 --> 00:27:16.050
You going to answer me or what?

00:27:16.170 --> 00:27:17.180
Answer what?

00:27:17.240 --> 00:27:18.420
What I said before.

00:27:18.480 --> 00:27:19.820
What was that?

00:27:19.930 --> 00:27:21.390
Weren't you listening?

00:27:21.940 --> 00:27:23.860
It's not like that!

00:27:23.950 --> 00:27:26.810
Never mind... Now run faster!

00:27:28.800 --> 00:27:33.200
omoide hitotsu nokosazuni kisetsu ga kawatta

00:27:28.800 --> 00:27:33.200
Without a single new memory, the season has changed.

00:27:33.500 --> 00:27:38.140
kimi ga shini futari ga umare aozora ga hirogaru

00:27:33.500 --> 00:27:38.140
You die, we are born, and the blue sky spreads out.

00:27:38.140 --> 00:27:42.610
kizutsuita tsubasa ga naze konnani mo ima

00:27:38.140 --> 00:27:42.610
My injured wings, I wonder why now

00:27:42.830 --> 00:27:44.900
tsuyoku kanjirarerun darou

00:27:42.830 --> 00:27:44.900
They feel so strong

00:27:45.180 --> 00:27:48.420
setsunasa mune ni aru noni

00:27:45.180 --> 00:27:48.420
even though I have sorrows in my heart.

00:27:47.630 --> 00:27:49.660
yasashisa no imi shirazuni

00:27:47.630 --> 00:27:49.660
The meaning of kindness never known to me

00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:52.010
atemonaku tada samayoi

00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:52.010
I just wander aimlessly.

00:27:52.360 --> 00:27:54.320
arasoukoto ga ikiteru

00:27:52.360 --> 00:27:54.320
The proof of life is fighting,

00:27:54.370 --> 00:27:58.790
oh, akashito shinjitetai

00:27:54.370 --> 00:27:58.790
Oh, this I want to believe

00:27:58.840 --> 00:28:04.380
kinouni say good bye today

00:27:58.840 --> 00:28:04.380
Say goodbye to yesterday today.

00:28:06.450 --> 00:28:11.040
"Mary's Buddies Birthday" sayonara kara

00:28:06.450 --> 00:28:11.040
"Maried Body's Birthday", With good-bye

00:28:11.160 --> 00:28:15.820
tsugi no watashi wo hajime taiyo

00:28:11.160 --> 00:28:15.820
Is where I want to start next time.

00:28:15.850 --> 00:28:20.500
"Mary's Buddies Birthday" dakishimetai

